       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change my concern. 12,750 mg/day is about five times the maximum daily dose, and I can't see any clinical scenario where that dose is safe. It could cause life-threatening lactic acidosis.\n\nYou can still get the order placed in a few ways:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** For example, I can enter 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum). A lower starting dose such as 500 mg twice daily is also an option.\n- **Have your resident or attending review it.** If they intend a dose outside standard limits, they can enter it directly and document the rationale. Pharmacy would also normally flag it.\n- **Check the source.** The number may have been mistyped or copied from somewhere else, such as a total in mg or a different drug.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
